const e="Psychodynamic Therapy | Michelle Barratt Psychology",t="Psychodynamic Therapy with Michelle Barratt Psychology in Toowong, Manly West and online Australia-wide.",a='<!--$--><section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-plum to-rose text-white"><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20"><div><nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-6"><ol class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-white/75"><li><a class="hover:text-white" href="/">Home</a></li><li aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3 w-3"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg></li><li><a class="hover:text-white active" href="/therapy-services" data-status="active" aria-current="page">Therapy Services</a></li><li aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3 w-3"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg></li><li class="text-white" aria-current="page">Psychodynamic Therapy</li></ol></nav><p class="text-[12px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-white/85 mb-3">Specialised Therapy</p><h1 class="text-white text-[32px] md:text-[44px] font-semibold leading-[1.08] max-w-3xl">Psychodynamic Therapy</h1><div class="h-[3px] w-16 bg-sun my-5" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="max-w-2xl text-[16px] md:text-[17px] text-white/95 space-y-3"></div><div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 bg-white text-plum hover:bg-blush " href="/contact">Contact Us</a><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 border border-white/70 text-white hover:bg-white/10 " href="/practitioners">See Practitioners</a></div></div></div></section><section class="bg-soft !py-0"><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="py-14 md:py-16"><img src="https://michellebarrattpsychology.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/online-therapy-in-brisbane-when-you-featured.webp" alt="Read more about the article Online Therapy in Brisbane When You Can&#x27;t Find Local Support" class="w-full aspect-[16/9] max-h-[520px] object-cover rounded border border-lilac"/></div></div></section><section class="bg-white "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">Psychodynamic Therapy in Brisbane: Making Sense of How You Feel</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><ul class="max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6"><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Post comments: 0 Comments</span></li></ul></div></section><section class="bg-soft "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">Seeing the Patterns Beneath How You Feel.</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Many adults look for support not because life is falling apart, but because something does not quite add up inside. Work might be fine, relationships might look ok from the outside, yet familiar feelings of anxiety, emptiness, or conflict keep repeating. It can be confusing to notice the same emotional or relationship patterns coming back, even when you are trying your best to do things differently.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Psychodynamic therapy is one way of gently making sense of these patterns. It focuses on the deeper emotional currents that sit underneath thoughts, feelings, and behaviour, and on how old experiences might still be shaping life today. At Michelle Barratt Psychology, we offer adult therapy services from our Brisbane clinics in Toowong and Manly West, and through online sessions across Australia. Wanting to understand yourself more deeply is a valid and common reason to seek professional support, and you do not need to be in crisis to benefit.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Article by Timothy Rach Bachelor of Psychological Science with Honours (University of Queensland) Master of Clinical Psychology (Queensland University of Technology)</p></div></section><section class="bg-white "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">What Psychodynamic Therapy Is and How It Works</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Psychodynamic therapy is an insight-oriented approach that looks at the links between your early experiences, relationships and your current emotional life. The idea is that we all develop ways of coping and relating that once helped us manage difficult feelings or situations, and some of these patterns continue automatically in adulthood.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">This is not about blaming your past or your family. It is about noticing how old strategies might still be operating, even when they are no longer helpful. For example, always putting other people first might have made sense in childhood, but in adult life it can lead to burnout or resentment.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">In psychodynamic therapy, we might explore themes such as:</p><ul class="max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6"><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Recurring relationship patterns that feel familiar but unsatisfying</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Anxiety or depression that is hard to explain logically</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Strong emotional reactions that seem bigger than the situation</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Shame, self-criticism, or feeling like you are never &quot;enough&quot;</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Difficulty trusting or relying on others</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Unresolved grief or trauma responses</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Questions about identity, self-worth or belonging</span></li></ul><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">The overall aim is to build self-awareness and a kinder understanding of yourself, so you have more flexible, healthy ways of responding to stress, relationships and life changes.</p></div></section><section class="bg-soft "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">When Psychodynamic Therapy May Be Especially Helpful</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Many people come to adult therapy services when they feel stuck in cycles that do not shift, even after trying to think positively or use coping tools. You might notice that you keep choosing similar partners, avoid conflict, then feel resentful, or feel overwhelmed for reasons that are not obvious.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Often, old coping strategies are quietly at work in the background. These can include:</p><ul class="max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6"><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>People-pleasing to keep the peace or avoid rejection</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Shutting down emotions to get through difficult situations</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Over-achieving to feel worthy or safe</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Keeping everything inside to avoid burdening others</span></li></ul><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">These patterns might have helped you feel safer at an earlier time in life, but they can now feed anxiety, depression, burnout or relationship difficulties. A psychodynamic approach helps connect the dots between what is happening now and deeper emotional themes that might not yet be fully conscious. This can be particularly useful if you have tried shorter-term or skills-focused therapies before and still sense that something underneath has not been addressed.</p></div></section><section class="bg-white "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">Looking Beneath Anxiety, Depression and Relationship Struggles</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Anxiety is often described as worry, but psychodynamic therapy views it as a signal that something deeper may be going on. Anxiety can be tied to fear of rejection or disapproval, fear of conflict, worries about losing control, or the impact of unresolved trauma. By exploring this in therapy, we can start to understand what your anxiety is trying to protect you from, and why certain situations feel especially threatening.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Depression can also have roots in long-standing patterns, such as always putting others first, carrying unspoken grief, feeling ashamed of your needs, or pushing down anger because it felt unsafe to express it. In a supportive therapeutic space, looking at these themes gradually can help ease emotional heaviness, not just manage symptoms on the surface.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Relationships are another area where psychodynamic therapy can be very helpful. You might notice patterns such as:</p><ul class="max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6"><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Feeling drawn to people who are unavailable or critical</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Pulling away when relationships become close</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Struggling with boundaries, either saying yes too often or shutting others out</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Being strongly triggered by particular tones, looks or behaviours</span></li></ul><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Exploring attachment style, fears about closeness, and earlier relationship experiences can shed light on why these patterns keep reappearing. Over time, this understanding can shift how you show up in friendships, family relationships and intimate partnerships, often allowing for more honesty and connection.</p></div></section><section class="bg-soft "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">Psychodynamic Therapy, CBT and Finding the Right Fit</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Cognitive Behavioural Therapy, or CBT, and psychodynamic therapy can both be effective, but they focus on different aspects of experience. CBT mainly looks at the here-and-now, helping you notice and change unhelpful thoughts and behaviours. It often includes structured exercises and practical strategies.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Psychodynamic therapy looks more at deeper emotional patterns, your history, and the ways you relate to yourself and others. A simple way to think about it is:</p><ul class="max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6"><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>CBT: What am I thinking and doing right now, and how can I change it?</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Psychodynamic: Why do I keep feeling and reacting this way, and where might it come from?</span></li></ul><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Some people respond very well to practical tools alone. Others find that combining CBT strategies with psychodynamic insight leads to more lasting change. Psychodynamic therapy may suit adults who want more than symptom relief, who are curious about their inner world, or who have long-standing patterns of distress or recurring conflict that do not shift easily.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">At Michelle Barratt Psychology, we discuss different approaches within our adult therapy services and work collaboratively to find a style that matches your goals, preferences and pace.</p></div></section><section class="bg-white "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">What to Expect and Accessing Therapy in Brisbane and Online</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">In a psychodynamic therapy session, you and your psychologist usually talk about what is happening in your life, how you are feeling, and what stands out to you from week to week. Over time, you might both start to notice themes, patterns and emotional responses that appear in different situations.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Your psychologist may invite reflections about:</p><ul class="max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6"><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Links between past and present experiences</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Inner conflicts, such as wanting closeness but fearing it</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Recurring dreams or images that seem meaningful</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Defence mechanisms, like joking, zoning out or minimising feelings</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>How you relate to your therapist, and how this might mirror other relationships</span></li></ul><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Therapy moves at your pace. You do not need to know where to start or have a clear story prepared. Feeling unsure, nervous or even sceptical at first is very normal, and can be talked about in the session.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">The length of therapy varies. Some people come for a shorter period to focus on a specific issue, while others choose longer-term work to explore deeper, long-standing patterns. This is something that can be discussed openly in your early sessions so you have a sense of what feels manageable.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Psychodynamic-informed adult therapy services are available at our Brisbane clinics in Toowong and Manly West, as well as through online therapy across Australia. Online sessions can be especially helpful if you live outside Brisbane, have busy work or parenting commitments, experience mobility difficulties, or simply prefer the privacy and convenience of telehealth.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">It may be time to consider support if you feel overwhelmed, stuck, emotionally numb, disconnected from yourself, or caught in patterns you cannot shift on your own. Psychodynamic therapy offers a way to explore what lies beneath the surface, so you can feel more grounded, more connected and more at home within yourself.</p></div></section><section class="bg-soft "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">Take The Next Step Toward Feeling More Like Yourself</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">If you are ready to explore what is going on beneath the surface, our adult therapy services can support you to make sense of your experiences and move toward meaningful change. At Michelle Barratt Psychology, we work with you at a pace that feels safe while still helping you make real progress. Reach out today so we can talk together about what you need and how we can best support you.</p></div></section><section class="bg-lilac !py-14"><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><p class="text-[12px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-rose mb-4">More in <!-- -->Specialised Therapy</p><ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-3"><li><a class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-white border border-lilac rounded px-4 py-2.5 text-[14px] font-medium text-ink transition-colors hover:border-ocean hover:text-ocean" href="/therapy-services/borderline-personality-disorder">Borderline Personality Disorder<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3.5 w-3.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg></a></li><li><a class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-white border border-lilac rounded px-4 py-2.5 text-[14px] font-medium text-ink transition-colors hover:border-ocean hover:text-ocean" href="/therapy-services/bipolar-disorder">Bipolar Disorder<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3.5 w-3.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg></a></li><li><a class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-white border border-lilac rounded px-4 py-2.5 text-[14px] font-medium text-ink transition-colors hover:border-ocean hover:text-ocean" href="/therapy-services/personality-disorders">Personality Disorders<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3.5 w-3.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg></a></li><li><a class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-white border border-lilac rounded px-4 py-2.5 text-[14px] font-medium text-ink transition-colors hover:border-ocean hover:text-ocean" href="/therapy-services/narcissistic-personality-disorder">Narcissistic Personality Disorder<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3.5 w-3.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg></a></li><li><a class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-white border border-lilac rounded px-4 py-2.5 text-[14px] font-medium text-ink transition-colors hover:border-ocean hover:text-ocean" href="/therapy-services/diabetes">Diabetes Mental Health Support<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3.5 w-3.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg></a></li><li><a class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-white border border-lilac rounded px-4 py-2.5 text-[14px] font-medium text-ink transition-colors hover:border-ocean hover:text-ocean" href="/therapy-services/eating-disorders">Eating Disorders<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3.5 w-3.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg></a></li></ul></div></section><section class="bg-blush"><div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-14 md:py-16 text-center"><p class="text-[12px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-rose mb-2.5">Take the first step</p><h2 class="text-[30px] md:text-[40px] font-semibold leading-[1.1]">Ready to Take the First Step?</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-4 mx-auto" aria-hidden="true"></div><p class="mt-5 text-[17px]">Seeking support can feel overwhelming, but you do not have to navigate life&#x27;s challenges alone. Our administration team can help answer your questions, explain appointment options and connect you with a suitable practitioner.</p><p class="mt-3">Prefer to call? Phone our administration team on <a class="text-ocean underline underline-offset-4 font-medium" href="tel:0731850040">07 3185 0040</a>.</p><div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3"><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 bg-rose text-white hover:bg-[#9d2a59] " href="/practitioners">Book Online</a><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 bg-ocean text-white hover:bg-[#095a6f] " href="/contact">Contact Us</a><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 border border-plum text-plum hover:bg-lilac  active" href="/therapy-services" data-status="active" aria-current="page">Explore Services</a></div><p class="mt-5 text-sm text-ink/70">If in crisis, please call 000.</p></div></section><!--/$-->',s={title:e,description:t,html:a};export{s as default,t as description,a as html,e as title};
